# Empathix

Monorepo with two apps:
- `FRONT/` — Next.js 15 + React 19 web app (port 3000). Screens, browser voice call (WebRTC), report, personal area.
- `BACK/` — Node 20 + Express 4 API (port 4000). Holds the OpenAI key, builds the employee and coach prompts, returns feedback and coach voice.

Before any change, read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root: it has the architecture, file map, run commands, env vars and the product rules.

Run everything: `npm run setup` once, then `npm run dev` from the root.
Before finishing a task: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` must pass.

Hard rules:
- The OpenAI key and all prompts stay in BACK. FRONT talks to BACK only through `FRONT/lib/api.ts`.
- `lib/types.ts` (FRONT) and `src/lib/types.ts` (BACK) must stay identical.
- Every UI string goes into `FRONT/lib/i18n.ts` in Hebrew, English and French.
- Hebrew is RTL: use logical CSS properties and check the Hebrew view.
- Coach feedback: no scores/labels/diagnoses, exact quotes only (keep `verifyQuote`), exactly three feedback rows.
- Mock mode (empty `OPENAI_API_KEY`) must keep working so the UI can be reviewed without cost.
